riscv: add a driver for the Sedna system controller

The Sedna RISC-V virtual machine powers off and resets through a small
system controller ("sedna,syscon"), and raises its interrupt when the host
asks the guest to power off or reboot. Its firmware has no SBI SRST
extension, so this is the only way to power the machine off.

Write the command register in shutdown_final, and turn host requests into
an orderly shutdown_nice(). Equivalent to the sedna-syscon driver of the
Sedna Linux tree.

